gb3F(){return'If your broker exports CSV but isn\'t auto-detected, tap the blue "Using a different broker?" banner, or tap "Map Columns Manually" after uploading the file.\n\nNote: OFX/QFX files from US brokers are always auto-detected and never need manual mapping.\n\nThe Column Mapper lets you tell the app which column is which:\n\u2022 Date column + date format (e.g. yyyy-MM-dd)\n\u2022 Quantity column\n\u2022 Transaction type (column or fixed value \u2014 buy/sell/dividend)\n\u2022 Stock identifier: Ticker, ISIN, or Name\n\u2022 Price: per-share or total amount\n\u2022 Currency: column or fixed (e.g. SEK)\n\nA live preview of the first rows helps you verify the mapping is correct.\n\nOnce set up, tap the bookmark icon to save the mapping as a template. Next time you upload a file from the same broker, the template is applied automatically.'},
gb3G(){return"generic, mapper, column mapping, manual, custom broker, unknown broker, CSV"},
gb3H(){return"Any broker's CSV can be imported by mapping columns manually \u2014 once."},
gb3I(){return"Using a Different Broker (Generic CSV Mapper)"},
gb3J(){return"VaR answers a specific question: based on your portfolio's actual past behaviour, what is the worst loss you would expect to see on 5% of days?\n\nMethod: Historical simulation\n1. Collect your daily portfolio values (recorded each time you refresh prices)\n2. Compute the % change in value from one recorded day to the next. Days when money moved in or out \u2014 a purchase, a sale, a past trade added, changed or removed, or a dividend (from 28 Sep 2026, where recorded) \u2014 are left out, so buying and selling do not count as gain or loss (an amount of up to 0.05% of the portfolio's value is too small to leave a day out)\n3. Sort all returns from worst to best\n4. Read the 5th percentile: leave out the worst 5% of returns (rounded down) and take the next one \u2014 with 20 returns that is the second-worst, with 40 the third-worst, and with fewer than 20 the worst\n\nExample: Daily VaR 2.3% means on your worst 5% of days, you lost at least 2.3%. If that return is not a loss, the card says \"No loss\".\n\nWeekly VaR = Daily VaR \xd7 \u221a5 when a value is recorded every trading day. When days are missing, each return covers more than one trading day, and the app scales by \u221a(5 \xf7 the average number of trading days per return) instead.\n\n\u26a0 VaR does NOT predict the maximum possible loss. Actual losses on extreme days can exceed VaR. It is a statistical estimate, not a guarantee.\n\nData builds automatically \u2014 the more days you use the app, the more reliable the estimate. 20+ data points (~1 month) are needed for a meaningful result."},
gb3K(){return"VaR, value at risk, risk, loss, percentile, confidence, 95%, daily, weekly"},
gb3L(){return"On a bad day or week (worst 5% of periods), how much could your portfolio lose?"},
gb3M(){return"When a tag is selected, VaR uses daily snapshots from the tag_daily_snapshots table \u2014 recorded automatically each time you open the app with stocks tagged.\n\nThe method:\n\u2022 Daily returns from the tag's value history \u2014 the plain change in value from one recorded day to the next\n\u2022 5th percentile of those returns\n\u2022 Weekly VaR = Daily \xd7 \u221a5, or \xd7 \u221a(5 \xf7 the average number of trading days per return) when days are missing\n\nUnlike the whole portfolio, a tag cannot leave out days when money moved in or out: tag history records no invested amount, so buying or selling inside the tag counts as a price move.\n\nNew tags start accumulating from the day they are created. You need ~20 daily app-opens (~1 month) for a reliable estimate.\n\nImportant: if you rename a tag, old snapshot history is lost for that tag name. Keep tag names stable."},
gb3N(){return"VaR, tag, sub-portfolio, filter, daily, snapshot"},
gb3O(){return"VaR also works per tag, using daily snapshots recorded separately for each sub-portfolio."},
gb3P(){return"VaR \u2014 Tag / Sub-Portfolio"},
gb3Q(){return"Volatility measures the standard deviation of your daily portfolio returns \u2014 how consistently or erratically your portfolio value changes.\n\nA higher number means bigger day-to-day swings:\n\ud83d\udfe2 Low (< 10%) \u2014 very stable, similar to a bond fund\n\ud83d\udfe1 Moderate (10\u201320%) \u2014 typical diversified equity portfolio\n\ud83d\udfe0 High (20\u201335%) \u2014 concentrated or growth-heavy portfolio\n\ud83d\udd34 Very High (> 35%) \u2014 highly concentrated or speculative holdings\n\nThe app uses a sample standard deviation (N\u22121 denominator) and scales it to annual using the standard 252 trading-days convention.\n\nDays when money moved in or out \u2014 a purchase, a sale, a past trade added, changed or removed, and a dividend (from 28 Sep 2026, where recorded) \u2014 are left out, so buying does not look like a gain and inflate the number (an amount of up to 0.05% of the portfolio's value is too small to leave a day out). A tag's history records no invested amount, so for a tag a one-day jump over 50% is left out instead.\n\nData builds automatically. 20+ daily data points (~1 month) are needed for a reliable estimate. The card shows a low-confidence warning below that threshold."},
gb3R(){return"volatility, sigma, standard deviation, risk, swing, fluctuation, annual"},
gb3S(){return"How much your portfolio value swings day-to-day, expressed as an annualised percentage."},
gb3T(){return"Volatility (\u03c3)"},
gb3U(){return"Every qualifying member can vote on open proposals.\n\nVote weight:\nYour vote is not equal to everyone else's \u2014 it is weighted by your qualifying hit count. A member with 10 qualifying hits has more influence than one with 3. The maximum weight is capped at 25 to prevent any single user from dominating.\n\nLink to stats:\nWhen voting Yes, you can optionally link the vote to your prediction stats. This publicly shows that you backed the proposal with your track record.\n\nVotes are permanent \u2014 you cannot change your vote after casting it.\n\nOnce approved, the proposal becomes a live position automatically. Proposals that do not reach the threshold before their deadline close without becoming positions."},
gb3V(){return"vote, voting, weight, yes, no, approve, proposal, track record, qualifying hits"},
gb3W(){return"Vote Yes or No on any open proposal. Your vote weight equals your qualifying hit count (max 25)."},
gb3X(){return"Voting on Proposals"},
gb3Y(){return'Add a stock and choose status "Watching".\n\nWatched stocks:\n\u2022 Appear in the Watching tab\n\u2022 Are tracked from the day you start watching (watchedPrice and watchedSince are set automatically)\n\u2022 Show up in the Opportunity Cost analysis \u2014 so you can see what return you missed\n\u2022 Can have Price Alerts set just like owned stocks\n\nWhen you decide to buy, edit the stock and change status to Owned, then log your buy transaction.'},
